# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Added 2026-08-04. This repo had NO .gitignore, which is why the deploy broke.
#
# `.next/` — the Next.js BUILD OUTPUT — was committed (65 files). A committed
# build directory ships a stale Server Action manifest, and Next resolves
# incoming action ids against it. That is the direct cause of the runtime flood:
#
#     Error: Failed to find Server Action "6607bb17".
#     This request might be from an older or newer deployment.
#
# The message is accurate and was pointing at the repo the whole time: the
# deployment really did contain actions from an older build, because the older
# build was checked in. Never commit .next/.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Build output
.next/
out/
build/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Dependencies
node_modules/
.pnp
.pnp.js

# Environment — .env and .env.local were TRACKED here. Both are empty at HEAD,
# but history at 5523937d (2026-04-17) carried a real TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN.
# Untracking is not rotation: that token is still in git history and should be
# rotated regardless of this file.
.env
.env*.local
.env.production
!.env.example

# Agent/tool scratch. A committed .claude/worktrees tree (including a nested
# copy of another repo) previously bloated the build context to 61.7 MB and made
# railpack discover phantom package.json files outside the project root.
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/settings.local.json

# Logs / OS / editor
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/

# Vercel / coverage
.vercel
coverage/
